matrix.tsv -- what this is and why it is versioned
====================================================

This is the COMBOS MATRIX: one row per in-scope combo (oracle.matrix.COMBOS),
recording which annotation flags real VEP was run with (`vep_flags`) and the
vepyr kwargs derived from them (`vepyr_kwargs`) -- see oracle/matrix.py's module
docstring for why the vepyr side is DERIVED rather than hand-written.

It is GENERATED, by bin/seed_matrix.py, from the `##VEP-command-line=` header
that real VEP wrote into each combo's ground-truth VCF. It is not source code;
it is a snapshot of what the ground truth (a multi-gigabyte tree that lives
only on the cluster, under $VEPYR_DATA/ground_truth_vep*/) actually contains.

Provenance of the copy in this repo:
  fetched from      hpc:~/vepyr/work/matrix.tsv
  fetched on        2026-08-02
  cluster mtime     2026-07-23 09:43 CEST
  size               5949 bytes
  sha256             28bc22fad3d8a129ec3f10b155f704353d73f2dc798b47e58eb6e522185ffa48

Why it is committed here instead of regenerated on demand: bin/seed_matrix.py
needs the ground truth to regenerate this file, and the ground truth is
multi-gigabyte -- a laptop, a CI runner, or a container build will not have it.
Without a copy checked into the repo, a fresh clone of this repo has no
matrix.tsv anywhere and bin/validate.py (and bin/run_wgs.py) cannot run at all,
which defeats the point of shipping the harness in a container image.

How it is found at runtime: bin/validate.py resolves MATRIX_PATH through a
fallback chain -- see the comment beside MATRIX_PATH in that file for the exact
order. In short: an explicit $VEPYR_MATRIX override wins if set; otherwise a
freshly-seeded $VEPYR_WORK/matrix.tsv on the cluster wins over this shipped
copy, so existing cluster behaviour is unchanged; this file is the fallback
that makes a fresh clone runnable at all.

This file is pinned `-text` in .gitattributes (it is CRLF, as fetched from the
cluster) so no checkout, on any machine or git config, can silently rewrite its
bytes -- see commit ed97de0 for the CRLF-drift bug class this guards against.
Do not hand-edit it; regenerate with bin/seed_matrix.py on the cluster and
re-fetch instead, so it always matches a real ground-truth run.
